===Etymology 1===
From {{bor|en|nl|baas}}, from {{der|en|dum|baes|t=master of a household, friend}}, from {{der|en|odt|*baso|t=uncle, kinsman}}, from {{der|en|gmw-pro|*baswō}}, from {{der|en|gem-pro|*baswô|t=uncle}}, perhaps from {{der|en|gem-pro|*bō-|*ba-, *bō-|t=father, older male relative}}, source also of the English terms {{m|en|babe}}, {{m|en|boy}}, {{m|en|bub}}, {{m|en|bully}}. [[cognate|Cognate]] with {{cog|gml|bās||supervisor, foreman}}, {{cog|ofs|bas||master}}, hence {{cog|stq|Boas|t=boss}}, {{cog|goh|basa||father's sister, cousin}}, hence German {{m|de|Base||aunt, cousin}}.

Originally a term of respect used to address an older relative. Later, in [[w:New Amsterdam|New Amsterdam]], it began to mean a person in charge who is not a master. The representation of Dutch ''-aa-'' by English ''-o-'' is due to the older unrounded pronunciation of this letter, which is still used in North America and parts of Ireland, but was formerly found in some British accents as well.

The video game sense is {{bor+|en|ja|ボス|tr=bosu|nocap=1}}, in turn from {{der|en|en|boss}}.

====Noun====
{{en-noun}}

# A person who oversees and directs the work of others; a [[supervisor]].
#* '''February 18, 2018''', Dawn Pine, ''[https://web.archive.org/web/20201001113213/https://www.returnofkings.com/152682/12-strategies-for-dealing-with-a-bad-boss Strategies for Dealing with a Bad Boss]''
#*: we have some vindictive people as '''bosses''', and you don’t want to be the target of their wrath.
# A person in charge of a [[business]] or [[company]].
#: {{syn|en|employer}}
#: {{ux|en|Chat turned to whisper when the '''boss''' entered the conference room.}}
#: {{ux|en|My '''boss''' complains that I'm always late to work.}}
# A [[leader]], the [[head]] of an organized [[group]] or [[team]].
#: {{syn|en|head|leader}}
#: {{ux|en|They named him '''boss''' because he had good leadership skills.}}
# The head of a [[political]] [[party]] in a given [[region]] or [[district]].
#: {{syn|en|leader}}
#: {{ux|en|He is the Republican '''boss''' in Kentucky.}}
# {{lb|en|informal|especially|India|MLE|and|Philippines}} {{non-gloss|A term of address to a man.}}
#: {{ux|en|Yes, '''boss'''.}}
# {{senseid|en|video games}} {{lb|en|video games}} An [[enemy]], often at the end of a [[level]], that is particularly challenging and must be beaten in order to progress.
#: {{syn|en|guardian}}
# {{lb|en|humorous}} [[wife|Wife]].
#: {{ux|en|There's no olive oil; will sunflower oil do? — I'll have to run that by the '''boss'''.}}

