# A [[swelling]], [[lump]] or [[protuberance]] in an animal, person or object.
#: {{cot|en|tuberosity}}
## {{lb|en|geology}} A lump-like mass of [[rock]], especially one projecting through a stratum of different rock.
## A convex protuberance in hammered work, especially the rounded projection in the centre of a [[shield]].
## {{senseid|en|prominence or projection on an object}} {{lb|en|mechanics}} A [[protrusion]]; frequently a [[cylinder]] of [[material]] that extends beyond a [[hole]].
##: {{cot|en|ear<id:prominence or projection on an object><!--usually coordinate; rarely synonymous-->|eye<id:loop or hole to receive hook or line, and integral with whole>}}
##* {{RQ:McCarthy Blood Meridian|chapter=IV|passage=The seargent {{...}} screwing a bipod into the threaded '''boss''' on the underside of the barrel would kill these animals {{...}}}}
## {{lb|en|architectural element}} A [[knob]] or [[projection]], usually at the [[intersection]] of [[rib]]s in a [[vault]].
## {{lb|en|architecture}} A roughly cut stone set in place for later carving.
# {{lb|en|archery}} A [[target]] block, made of foam but historically made of hay bales, to which a target face is attached.
# A wooden vessel for the mortar used in tiling or masonry, hung by a hook from the laths, or from the rounds of a ladder.
#* {{quote-book|en|year=1842|author=Peter Nicholson|title=The Mechanic's Companion|passage='''Boss''', a short trough for holding water, when tiling the roof}}
# A [[head]] or [[reservoir]] of [[water]].

